[32m +# Member 4 — Database[m
[32m +[m
[32m +## CitizenCare Complaint Management System[m
[32m +[m
[32m +This folder is the database deliverable for **Member 4**. It contains the database architecture, table definitions, relationships, demo/seed data, and database documentation.[m
[32m +[m
[32m +### Files[m
[32m +[m
[32m +- `schema.sql` — Creates the MySQL database, tables, constraints, indexes, and relationships.[m
[32m +- `seed.sql` — Inserts demo administrators, departments, employees, and complaints.[m
[32m +- `README.md` — Database documentation and setup instructions.[m
[32m +[m
[32m +## Database[m
[32m +[m
[32m +**DBMS:** MySQL 8+[m
[32m +[m
[32m +**Database name:** `citizen_complaints`[m
[32m +[m
[32m +### Tables[m
[32m +[m
[32m +1. **admins** — administrator login/account data.[m
[32m +2. **departments** — government/service departments.[m
[32m +3. **employees** — workers assigned to departments.[m
[32m +4. **complaints** — citizen complaints, status, assignment, priority, and AI classification results.[m
[32m +[m
[32m +### Relationships[m
[32m +[m
[32m +- `employees.department_id` → `departments.id`[m
[32m +- `complaints.department_id` → `departments.id`[m
[32m +- `complaints.employee_id` → `employees.id`[m
[32m +[m
[32m +The foreign keys use `ON DELETE SET NULL`, so removing a department or employee does not delete historical complaints.[m
[32m +[m
[32m +### Complaint / AI fields[m
[32m +[m
[32m +The `complaints` table stores:[m
[32m +[m
[32m +- Citizen name and email[m
[32m +- Complaint title and description[m
[32m +- Original category[m
[32m +- `ai_category` for AI classification[m
[32m +- `severity` (`Low`, `Medium`, `High`, `Critical`)[m
[32m +- `priority_score` (0–100)[m
[32m +- Location and optional image path[m
[32m +- Complaint status (`Pending`, `In Progress`, `Resolved`, `Rejected`, `Reopened`)[m
[32m +- Department and employee assignment[m
[32m +- Created and resolved timestamps[m
[32m +[m
[32m +### User storage[m
[32m +[m
[32m +The current backend has two account types:[m
[32m +[m
[32m +- `admins` for administrators[m
[32m +- `employees` for workers[m
[32m +[m
[32m +Citizen identity/contact information is currently stored with each complaint (`citizen_name`, `citizen_email`) because the existing backend does not use a separate citizen account table. This keeps the schema compatible with the current APIs.[m
[32m +[m
[32m +## Setup in MySQL / XAMPP[m
[32m +[m
[32m +1. Start **MySQL** in XAMPP.[m
[32m +2. Open phpMyAdmin or the MySQL command line.[m
[32m +3. Run `schema.sql` first.[m
[32m +4. Run `seed.sql` second.[m
[32m +5. Configure the backend `.env` values:[m
[32m +[m
[32m +```env[m
[32m +DB_HOST=localhost[m
[32m +DB_USER=root[m
[32m +DB_PASSWORD=[m
[32m +DB_PORT=3306[m
[32m +DB_NAME=citizen_complaints[m
[32m +```[m
[32m +[m
[32m +6. Start the backend from the `backend` folder.[m
[32m +[m
[32m +The existing `backend/db.js` also creates the MySQL schema automatically when `initializeDatabase()` is used.[m
[32m +[m
[32m +## Demo accounts[m
[32m +[m
[32m +Admin:[m
[32m +[m
[32m +- Email: `admin@gmail.com`[m
[32m +- Password: `admin123`[m
[32m +[m
[32m +Demo worker password:[m
[32m +[m
[32m +- `worker123`[m
[32m +[m
[32m +## Backend coordination note[m
[32m +[m
[32m +The schema intentionally matches the current MySQL structure used by `backend/db.js` and the complaint/auth/worker/dashboard API queries. Before changing columns, status values, or foreign-key relationships, coordinate with the Backend member because those API queries depend on these names and values.[m
[32m +[m
[32m +### Important current-project note[m
[32m +[m
[32m +The repository also contains `backend/server.js`, which includes a separate SQLite implementation (`backend/data/citizencare.sqlite`). The MySQL schema in this folder is aligned with `backend/db.js` and the Express route files. The team should use **one database implementation consistently** before the final integration/demo; do not maintain MySQL and SQLite as two competing production databases.[m
